Verdict: PASS, written to session_plan/eval_task_1.md.

What the test measures. The new test is tests/skills_fence_request.rs. It runs the real binary against a stub provider and counts a planted canary token in the request body the stub receives. I re-ran it and it printed these counts:

| Fixture | No fence | Deny | Allow proj |
|---|---|---|---|
| .yoyo/skills symlinked into secret/ | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| Plain .yoyo/skills/canary | 1 | 0 | — |
| --skills <secret>/skills | 1 | 0 | — |

The no-fence column is the required control: the canary does show up when nothing is fenced, so the deny zeros mean something. The pre-fix readings (deny = 1 in every shape) are in ARCHITECTURE.md and I didn't reproduce them myself.

What the fix does. Before loading any skill directory, yoyo now checks it with admit_skill_dir in the new src/skill_fence.rs. That calls DirectoryRestrictions::check_path on each SKILL.md and judges a symlink by where it points.
• **Coverage:** both the --skills flag directories and the auto-discovered ones go through this check.
• **Warning:** a refused directory prints a stderr warning, and every interpolated string goes through sanitize_for_display.
• **Near misses:** with --allow-dir proj, or a deny on an unrelated directory, the request body is exactly the same as the unfenced one.
• **Whole directory:** yoagent can't drop single skills from a loaded set, so a directory with any refused skill isn't loaded at all. The warning and the docs both say this.

Other checks:
• **Nothing left dangling:** the new module is registered in main.rs, and both callers of the changed auto_discover_skills signature were updated.
• **Moved call:** `parse_permission_and_dir_config` now runs earlier so skills can be fenced. Its old binding was removed cleanly, and it still runs before the project-context load.
• Docs: docs/src/configuration/permissions.md and the ARCHITECTURE.md entry were updated, and CLAUDE.md was correctly left alone.
• **Default behaviour:** with no --deny-dir or --allow-dir, the check skips everything, so the default path is unchanged.

Two minor gaps, not grounds to fail:
• **/doctor:** its skill audit still lists fenced directories on the terminal. ARCHITECTURE.md records this, and nothing it prints is sent to the model.
• **Positive control:** I didn't re-run the "neuter the check, watch the deny tests fail" control the task required. I only saw it recorded in ARCHITECTURE.md.

